WEBVTT

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:23.790
Your initials I wrote in my notebook

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:31.600
Discreetly overlapping so they won't be noticed

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:37.110
I stretched up

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:42.110
The school building I looked up at and the distant sky

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:53.690
The moon in broad daylight shows some restraint and lingers inside the light.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:01:01.310
I want these feelings to reach you

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.520
my heart

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:11.500
I embrace the small bud of passion that sprouted in my heart

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:13.880
I close my eyes

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:18.170
Some day I want to make it bloom into a big flower

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:15.750
someday

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:26.940
Our fluttering hearts connected, our eyes exchanging a glance

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:55.040
Every last one of them's got that lovey dovey face.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.650
What's wrong with that? It's Christmas, after all.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:02.280
Well, today is a pretty special day for couples.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:05.160
But you know, no matter how much time they spend on romance,

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.180
they're all looking for the same ending.

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:10.100
Mind back in the gutter so soon?

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:15.740
Then the girl says to the guy, "I'm your present for tonight."

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:20.640
I want a present like that, too.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.700
Girls like that don't actually exist...

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:23.910
Hey! Ichitaka, look!

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:29.790
When I find a girlfriend, I want to shop for underwear like that!

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:32.540
Calm down.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:35.930
Those are the same ones that Itsuki was wearing.

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:38.370
Huh? Is something wrong with Itsuki-chan?

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:40.180
It's nothing.

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:44.090
In the midst of my unrequited love,

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:46.850
Itsuki, my childhood friend, suddenly showed up.

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:50.120
I hadn't seen her in four years...

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:53.190
...and she'd become a frustrating temptress.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.060
Icchan? Is that you? It's been so long!

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.870
H-Hey! How do you know my name?!

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:08.480
Don't tell me you've forgotten the face of your fiancée!

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.480
You couldn't be...

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:18.610
...Itsuki?

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:22.160
Yes! Icchan!

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:24.850
Hey! Get your hands off me!

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.520
What's going on?! What are you doing here?!

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:33.770
I'll explain that later! Before that, I need the toilet!

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:37.230
Wait a second!

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:39.360
Hey, Icchan!

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:49.500
I'm in big trouble if she sees us like this!

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:05.310
Seto-kun?

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:07.890
Geez, Icchan!

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.920
I got excited for a second there. I thought you were going to attack me!

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:13.290
Don't be an idiot! This isn't the time for jokes.

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:15.930
Damn! It's locked.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:19.920
I can't hold it in. I'm going to pee my pants!

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.730
Just hang on a little longer.

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:23.140
Can I do it here?

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:24.540
What wrong with you?!

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:25.820
I'm joking.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:31.460
What is it?

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:34.870
Put this on for now. You can't walk around like that.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:40.250
Oh, Icchan, you're so kind! You've grown up a little, haven't you?

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.530
Shh! Be quiet!

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:45.240
But why are we sneaking around?

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:49.260
Your parents said I'd be welcome.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:52.600
We're expecting an <i>extra</i> special guest tomorrow.

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:56.160
So that's what she meant...

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.610
I-It's coming...

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:00.520
Itsuki, wait a second!

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:11.790
Did you go?

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:15.790
That was close. It was right at the exit.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:23.490
By the way, what are you doing here?

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:26.590
Didn't you move to America with your family?

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:28.950
What's with the attitude?

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:31.650
Should I not have come back?

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:33.470
That's not really what I meant.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:36.910
Then why can't you be a little more excited to see me?

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:40.290
We haven't seen each other in four years,

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:43.900
yet you're treating me like an inconvenience...

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:50.920
Itsuki, I'm sorry.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.490
I think I peed a little...

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.750
Listen. This is a really critical moment for me.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:59.480
I've finally got a chance with someone I've liked for a really long time.

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:02.380
So right now I'm trying to give it my best shot and tell her my feelings.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:05.670
I'll try and get her out of the house quickly.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:08.160
Could you stay out here for just a little longer?

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:09.440
I see.

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:12.350
There's a girl here.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.700
What best shot?! You liar!

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:21.610
Why are you out here sneaking around?!

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:25.510
If you like someone, then confess your feelings like a man!

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:32.120
I'm sorry. I heard voices.

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:35.430
Well... This is... I was just...

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:37.190
I'll go home for today.

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:43.090
This is bad... How much do you think she heard?

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:44.790
Like I'd know!

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:47.320
She might know how I feel about her.

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:49.880
You were going to confess anyway, right?

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:52.280
What should I do?

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:55.100
Ah! Toilet! Toilet!

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:58.440
It's already happened. There's nothing you can do about it.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:00.500
All you can do is keep going!

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.350
Why don't you follow her and walk her home?

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:12.950
Yoshizuki...

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:16.950
I left my cell phone here.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.620
Why didn't you tell me?

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:25.930
She's the girl from the photo, isn't she?

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:28.530
Uh, well, that's...

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.450
Did she come back from America?

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.190
Early this morning...

00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:35.220
That's amazing.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.540
She came to see you right after she came back to Japan.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:41.360
I bet she really wanted to see you, Seto-kun.

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:48.320
That's got nothing to do with you, Yoshizuki!

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:51.320
Sorry.

00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:58.800
There I go again...

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:10.620
What happened to our dramatic reunion?

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:12.340
Stupid Ichitaka.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:23.390
Nishi Eifuku Station

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:15.440
Thank you for walking with me.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:16.320
Sure.

00:08:19.670 --> 00:08:23.390
Seto-kun, she's waiting for you to confess.

00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:29.980
She said, "If you like someone, then confess your feelings like a man!"

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:32.150
Well, that is...

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:35.800
If you don't do it properly, it'll be a shame.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:42.160
That wasn't really what she meant.

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:57.540
She brought you these as a gift right? I dug in already.

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:00.350
You can have my half, too.

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:02.380
What? Did she reject you?

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:04.920
I never even got that far.

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:07.710
She thought we were talking about our relationship.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:09.520
It's not like she's wrong.

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:12.240
Did you already forget?

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:15.450
We promised to get married.

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:18.890
I came back for that.

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:20.360
W-Wait a second!

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:23.620
We were just little school children back then!

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:24.770
How cruel!

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:29.560
I've spent every day thinking about you for four years!

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:32.800
How could you forget such an important promise?

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:35.830
Hey, Itsuki, calm down.

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:38.260
You don't have to cry.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:41.470
Just kidding!

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:47.800
You think I'd marry an insensitive pig like you?

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:51.230
I'm just staying here until I find my own place.

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:58.530
Don't mess with people when they're suffering!

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:12.380
Anyway, I have to fix Iori-chan's misunderstanding somehow.

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:18.710
See! They all want to be in your fan club!

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:21.600
Will you give us your blessing?

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:28.600
All those guys... and they all like Iori-chan.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:35.990
Seto-kun!

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:38.070
Are you here to practice for the Welcome Party act?

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:40.610
Let's go!

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:44.120
Who's that guy?!

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:44.120
Who's he?

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:58.350
I'm sorry I got you involved in this.

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:01.060
But wow! A fan club, huh?

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:03.310
It feels like a problem.

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:05.180
Those guys probably think I'm your...

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:07.340
<i>That</i> would be a problem!

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:10.300
You don't have to be quite so harsh about it...

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:12.480
Your girlfriend's going to hate me.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:13.400
What?

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:18.520
Hey, Yoshizuki, the girl you saw yesterday is...

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:20.110
Oh, Icchan!

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:22.820
Itsuki?

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:26.490
Teratani, why are you two together?

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:30.620
I saw her wandering around the school not even wearing a uniform.

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:34.010
So I asked her what she was doing and she told me she was looking for you.

00:11:34.010 --> 00:11:37.740
Icchan, you have a good friend.

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:39.850
Why can't you just mind your own business?

00:11:39.850 --> 00:11:42.130
Oh, nice to see you again.

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:44.570
What are you doing here?

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:48.470
Why? I just wanted to see my darling's school.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:51.560
Darling?! Ichitaka, don't tell me you guys are-

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:55.180
Itsuki, don't say things like that! People might get the wrong idea.

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:57.380
Don't be shy, Icchan!

00:11:57.380 --> 00:12:00.450
We're already living in the same house.

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:02.820
But you're just freeloading until you find your own apartment.

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:06.070
It's not easy living with a pervert like Icchan.

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:10.380
He peeps at me in the bath and he attacks me in my sleep.

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:12.800
She's just making an American-style joke!

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:16.340
Don't be embarrassed! You're so cute.

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:19.350
Why don't you just go home now?

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:21.870
We have to go to class.

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:24.240
Then I'll wait here.

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:27.190
I have so many things I want to buy. Can you go shopping with me?

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:29.180
Why don't you go by yourself?

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:33.560
What do you mean by that? Is that any way to talk to your fiancée?

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:34.520
Fiancée?!

00:12:36.370 --> 00:12:39.440
Itsuki, just cut it out! You're really pissing me off!

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:42.850
You don't have to get so angry!

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:45.990
All right, I'm leaving.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:47.940
Iori-san, see you later.

00:12:47.940 --> 00:12:49.160
Oh, Itsuki-chan!

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:51.800
Is that okay, Seto-kun?

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:53.790
Just leave that little brat alone.

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:56.680
But, you shouldn't send your girlfriend away like that.

00:12:57.430 --> 00:13:00.670
You know, I think you've got the wrong idea about us.

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:04.150
Itsuki and I are just childhood friends.

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:05.300
Right, Itsuki?

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:08.050
I guess so.

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:09.850
See?

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:14.640
That's the way you feel, isn't it Icchan?

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:18.860
What? What does that mean?

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:21.860
It means...

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:24.860
I like you, Icchan!

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:36.290
What are you talking about? Stop making stuff up!

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:38.460
Why are you getting so angry at me?!

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:41.460
Are you having that much fun messing around with me like this?!

00:13:41.810 --> 00:13:44.960
Are you saying my feelings for you annoy you?

00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:46.850
Yes, it annoys me!

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:54.550
Man, you're so boring!

00:13:54.550 --> 00:13:58.500
You can't even take a little joke!

00:13:58.500 --> 00:13:59.800
You jerk!

00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:04.700
What a pain. Messing around with me like that.

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:08.450
I wonder if it was really a joke?

00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:11.700
It didn't look that way to me.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:17.010
What are you talking about? She lives to give me a hard time.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:20.320
So you know everything about her then?

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:23.920
The more you fight, the closer you become, right?

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:36.770
Thanks to Itsuki's return, I lost my chance to get close to Iori-chan.

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:41.210
The Ninin-baori act for the Welcoming Party also failed.

00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:50.080
What?

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:52.950
Just what are you staring at?

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:55.350
You look like a complete pervert.

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:57.130
I'm not staring at anything!

00:14:57.130 --> 00:15:00.300
Don't talk to me. They'll think we know each other.

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:01.710
Wait, Teratani!

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:11.040
This movie is...

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:14.840
Itsuki was part of the staff for this movie.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:16.700
Really?

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:18.980
She's trying to become a professional sculptor.

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:21.920
Her work is pretty good.

00:15:22.430 --> 00:15:26.190
I see, the movie's being released in Japan.

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:28.240
What are you getting so excited about?

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:31.470
You were always like that.

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:36.990
You were more relaxed and cheerful around Itsuki than with Yoshizuki.

00:15:41.630 --> 00:15:43.050
That's right.

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:47.490
Itsuki was like the sun that always shone on me.

00:15:47.490 --> 00:15:50.370
She was innocent and always true to her feelings.

00:15:50.870 --> 00:15:53.160
That's why I didn't realise the true feelings...

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:57.510
...that she hid deep inside her heart.

00:16:00.820 --> 00:16:03.170
Hey, why don't you help me?

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:07.510
Unlike yours, Icchan, my body is very delicate.

00:16:07.510 --> 00:16:12.150
Why did you have to rent the apartment just across from my house?

00:16:12.730 --> 00:16:15.990
I thought you'd miss me if I moved too far away.

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:27.920
Itsuki, this is the last one.

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:30.340
Thank you.

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:33.550
What are you wearing?!

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:36.220
Do you want to see what's underneath?

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:40.840
Did that surprise you?

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:45.970
Don't tease me any more!

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:49.540
Hey, don't be so rough with those!

00:16:49.540 --> 00:16:51.560
It's got important sculptures inside!

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:53.240
Sculptures?

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:54.430
Want to see them?

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:55.640
Not really.

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:57.160
You want to see them really, right?

00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:00.440
No, I'm not interested at all.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:04.020
Say "I want to see!"

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:07.940
All right! I get it! Let me go!

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:10.310
You are so stubborn.

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:15.470
Here.

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:20.990
How is it? Not bad, huh?

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:24.740
Actually, I'm kind of surprised that you make stuff like this.

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:29.990
My next door neighbour was a somewhat famous professional sculptor, working in Hollywood.

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:33.240
He got me into it.

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:35.260
Hey, speaking of which...

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:38.910
...didn't you make a clay bust of me a long time ago?

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:47.040
Wow! Did you make this? You're incredible!

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:50.260
Wow! That's the first nice thing you've ever said to me!

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:52.750
I'll treasure it forever!

00:17:54.430 --> 00:17:56.380
Do you still have it?

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:58.230
What? No way!

00:17:58.230 --> 00:18:00.010
That was forever ago.

00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:05.150
Why? You said you'd treasure it forever.

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:06.180
Are you disappointed?

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:09.650
Not really. It's not the kind of thing you'd hang on to.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:12.650
Say, what's been going on with Iori-san since then?

00:18:14.310 --> 00:18:16.530
Everything's back to square-one.

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:21.960
After the New Student Welcoming Party, I didn't have any reason to talk to her.

00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:24.930
Well, she was out of my league anyway.

00:18:24.930 --> 00:18:28.060
I don't think I'm good enough for her.

00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:30.420
What are you talking about? That's pathetic.

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:34.890
If you really like her, things like whether or not you're good enough for her don't matter.

00:18:34.890 --> 00:18:38.790
The most important thing is how much you care about her!

00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:42.110
You're just scared of being rejected!

00:18:42.110 --> 00:18:44.260
You're just being a coward!

00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:49.080
You have no right to say that!

00:18:49.080 --> 00:18:51.960
Besides, you jerked me around and messed up the situation,

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:54.190
so now my relationship with Iori-chan is just awkward.

00:18:54.490 --> 00:18:58.630
See, there you go blaming other people and running away again.

00:18:58.630 --> 00:19:01.360
Icchan, you have to tell her how you feel about her.

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:03.450
Otherwise, how will she ever know?

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:06.520
You don't understand my feelings.

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:11.140
You're always so straightforward.

00:19:11.140 --> 00:19:13.290
How could you understand how I feel?

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:24.220
Of course I understand.

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:36.150
Received Calls

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:36.150
Yoshizuki Iori

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:14.480
Yoshizuki?!

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:19.710
Seto-kun, do you anything planned for free time tomorrow?

00:20:20.390 --> 00:20:21.980
Well, not really.

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:23.050
I see.

00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:24.450
Why?

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:29.950
I was hoping you might be able to spend time with me.

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:32.960
You mean just the two of us?

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:35.720
I guess you don't want to.

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:37.470
No, I'd like to!

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:40.410
If it's all right with you, I'd love to.

00:20:40.410 --> 00:20:41.660
Really?!

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:45.850
What are you guys doing here?

00:20:45.850 --> 00:20:48.220
Could it be a secret rendezvous?

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:49.770
No way!

00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:52.170
Suspicious!

00:20:52.170 --> 00:20:55.060
If I didn't know better, I'd think you guys were dating!

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:57.060
They might be!

00:20:57.060 --> 00:20:58.850
It's definitely a rendezvous!

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:26.180
I'm sorry. I'm late.

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:27.680
Did you get out without any problems?

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:28.750
Yes.

00:21:28.750 --> 00:21:32.120
I told them I had an upset stomach, so I wanted to rest in my room.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:35.560
We don't know what they'll say if they find out about this.

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:38.940
Then, why don't we go somewhere that nobody would go?

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:47.570
I came to Kyoto once before...

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:49.760
...and I found the shrine.

00:21:49.760 --> 00:21:54.700
It's very small and unknown, but very beautiful.

00:21:56.840 --> 00:22:00.220
You're right. This place is really hidden.

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:16.670
Wow! It's so beautiful!

00:22:16.670 --> 00:22:19.470
Right?! Are you glad you came?

00:22:19.470 --> 00:22:21.060
Uh, yes.

00:22:21.990 --> 00:22:23.400
I'm so glad!

00:22:24.370 --> 00:22:28.400
I really wanted you to see this place.

00:22:57.330 --> 00:22:58.820
Shall we go?

00:22:58.820 --> 00:22:59.690
Yeah.

00:23:01.260 --> 00:23:03.170
I see.

00:23:03.170 --> 00:23:06.070
This is the shrine to the god of new love.

00:23:06.070 --> 00:23:09.060
"Men and women who lock their arms with each other and walk under these Torii...

00:23:09.060 --> 00:23:11.240
...will have their relationship develop into everlasting love."

00:23:11.240 --> 00:23:12.560
Sounds like fun. Let's do it!

00:23:12.560 --> 00:23:13.590
Yeah!

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:21.140
Oh, I didn't realise there was something like this.

00:23:26.570 --> 00:23:30.510
If we could walk under these three Torii, I may be able to find my courage.

00:23:32.380 --> 00:23:34.040
Seto-kun?

00:23:34.040 --> 00:23:35.310
Hey, Yoshizuki,

00:23:35.860 --> 00:23:38.890
since we're here, why don't we give it a go?

00:23:43.600 --> 00:23:44.960
I guess so.

00:23:45.460 --> 00:23:47.890
It could be a good memory of our school trip.

00:23:58.360 --> 00:24:01.870
Sorry... but the rule says we have to.

00:24:23.930 --> 00:24:25.090
Hello?

00:24:25.090 --> 00:24:26.740
Ichitaka! It's terrible!

00:24:26.740 --> 00:24:28.480
There's a fire at Itsuki-chan's!

00:24:28.940 --> 00:24:31.940
The apartment's gone up in flames and Itsuki-chan's no-

00:24:33.790 --> 00:24:37.420
Why the hell does the battery have to die at a time like this?!

00:24:38.040 --> 00:24:39.620
What's wrong?

00:24:39.620 --> 00:24:43.470
Itsuki's apartment caught fire and she's nowhere to be found...

00:24:43.980 --> 00:24:46.200
You should hurry home!

00:24:47.040 --> 00:24:50.540
But, I'm sure she was able to get out from the apartment.

00:24:51.600 --> 00:24:53.050
Never mind. Let's keep walking.

00:24:55.220 --> 00:24:56.780
It was Itsuki-chan.

00:24:57.980 --> 00:25:00.130
She helped me to do this.

00:25:00.890 --> 00:25:02.180
What do you mean?

00:25:02.180 --> 00:25:05.160
Itsuki-chan called me and told me...

00:25:05.160 --> 00:25:09.930
...you were very disappointed after our Ninin-baori act failed.

00:25:09.930 --> 00:25:10.990
That's why...

00:25:12.140 --> 00:25:15.940
Then, the reason why you asked me out today was...

00:25:15.940 --> 00:25:18.380
I'm sorry I didn't tell you.

00:25:18.380 --> 00:25:22.060
That idiot... She didn't have to do this.

00:25:22.060 --> 00:25:27.810
And she told me that you and her are just childhood friends.

00:25:30.500 --> 00:25:33.740
Hey, I think you'd better hurry up and go.

00:25:34.360 --> 00:25:35.640
But...

00:25:35.640 --> 00:25:39.100
Aren't you worried about Itsuki-chan?

00:25:47.720 --> 00:25:49.220
I'm sorry, Yoshizuki!

00:26:04.340 --> 00:26:05.330
Itsuki!

00:26:07.080 --> 00:26:10.130
Icchan, what are you doing here?

00:26:10.570 --> 00:26:12.980
My mum called me.

00:26:12.980 --> 00:26:16.130
She was worried that something might have happened to you in the fire.

00:26:16.620 --> 00:26:19.370
I see. I'm sorry.

00:26:19.370 --> 00:26:22.010
It's okay as long as you're all right.

00:26:23.040 --> 00:26:26.140
But, everything is burned up.

00:26:26.480 --> 00:26:29.340
You can stay at my place for a while.

00:26:35.790 --> 00:26:37.150
Itsuki?

00:26:48.380 --> 00:26:51.210
Itsuki, is that...?

00:26:52.240 --> 00:26:54.270
You found out, huh?

00:26:56.290 --> 00:26:57.630
To tell you the truth... I...

00:26:58.130 --> 00:27:01.090
...I've been treasuring it this whole time.

00:27:07.030 --> 00:27:08.070
Itsuki...

00:27:51.390 --> 00:27:59.040
The worn-out diary

00:27:59.040 --> 00:28:06.680
I left behind in a corner of the classroom

00:28:06.680 --> 00:28:15.120
I closed it softly. I hold this throbbing in my heart

00:28:15.120 --> 00:28:25.920
In both hands and warm it up

00:28:25.920 --> 00:28:33.160
Since that day I met you by chance,

00:28:33.160 --> 00:28:40.820
I've grown small wings

00:28:40.820 --> 00:28:48.210
I felt your kind gaze,

00:28:48.210 --> 00:28:56.180
And even now I have a feeling I could fly into the sky

00:28:56.180 --> 00:28:59.770
Staring eyes and eyes
